From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:03:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] test(ysk): wait for the cards instead of sleeping

The YSK tests slept a fixed second after starting the service and after
each publish, and failed under load (e.g. a parallel nix build). They
now re-publish the idempotent upsert/delete until the expected cards
are there, with a 10 s deadline, and count only their own card ids: the
in-memory repository is a shared-cache database, so other tests' cards
are visible too.

Stacked on "fix(service): startup races in the event and action
dispatch" (without it the subscription can still be lost at startup).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pkg/ysk/ysk_test.go | 97 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/ysk/ysk_test.go b/pkg/ysk/ysk_test.go
index 1975065..ea683ce 100644
--- a/pkg/ysk/ysk_test.go
+++ b/pkg/ysk/ysk_test.go
@@ -39,6 +39,36 @@ func mockPublish(ctx context.Context, sourceID string, eventName string, body ma
 	}
 }
 
+// eventually re-runs publish until the cards with the given ids number want:
+// the bus drops an event its dispatch loop is not ready to receive, and both
+// the upsert and the delete here are idempotent. It replaces fixed sleeps,
+// which failed under load. Only the given ids count: the in-memory repository
+// is a shared-cache database, so other tests' cards are visible too.
+func eventually(t *testing.T, yskService *service.YSKService, ids []string, want int, publish func()) {
+	t.Helper()
+	deadline := time.Now().Add(10 * time.Second)
+	for {
+		publish()
+		cards, err := yskService.YskCardList(context.Background())
+		assert.NilError(t, err)
+		got := 0
+		for _, card := range cards {
+			for _, id := range ids {
+				if card.Id == id {
+					got++
+				}
+			}
+		}
+		if got == want {
+			return
+		}
+		if time.Now().After(deadline) {
+			t.Fatalf("cards %v = %d, want %d", ids, got, want)
+		}
+		time.Sleep(20 * time.Millisecond)
+	}
+}
